                <pb facs="1066" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/59</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-03">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 4, 5:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>718. Suggest that there should be an international agreement if possible as to
                    just what each nation should give its prisoners of war, nature of food and
                    clothing; for instance. British claim they give overcoats, suits, underclothes,
                    socks, shoes, etc:, and three blankets to all prisoners, civil and military,
                    while here I have had to buy clothes etc., for English prisoners and they have
                    only two blankets, and our Ambassador, Paris, telegraphs Germans in French camps
                    badly in need of clothes. Many Russians here, I am told by Spanish Ambassador,
                    have no blankets. Authorities here have refused to allow me to give seven marks
                    a week to civil prisoners to allow them to get extra food.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1190-a1.xml" xpointer="d1190-a1"/>
